"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T06:09:23-07:00","id":1453540,"title":"","content":"Is it worth reading? Hasn\u2019t the setting changed drastically since the Nineties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T06:22:45-07:00","id":1453542,"title":"","content":"The setting ended a couple years after the website stopped being updated (last update was in 2000; the \u201cend of the world\u201d was in 2003); so in terms of pre-20th Anniversary Edition material, it's surprisingly not that out of date. But it <i>is</i> pre-20A stuff; so you should read it with that in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T06:48:49-07:00","id":1453545,"title":"","content":"Bringing this back to the original topic, here's the B.J. Zanzibar's World of Darkness article about the <a href=\"http://167.99.155.149/archive/time_lords_2.html\" target=\"_blank\">Time Lords</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-26-2021, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T10:54:00-07:00","id":1453566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453418-timelords?p=1453545#post1453545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing this back to the original topic, here's the B.J. Zanzibar's World of Darkness article about the <a href=\"http://167.99.155.149/archive/time_lords_2.html\" target=\"_blank\">Time Lords</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its pretty cool. Amusingly its probably underpowered compared to what some of the pre-revival novels and the revival show would let you get away with in terms of psychic powers and regeneration. In particular dismemberment/decapitation and most forms of WoD agg Damage wouldn't stop a timelord regeneration event nowadays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T20:33:48-07:00","id":1454171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453418-timelords?p=1453566#post1453566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its pretty cool. Amusingly its probably underpowered compared to what some of the pre-revival novels and the revival show would let you get away with in terms of psychic powers and regeneration. In particular dismemberment/decapitation and most forms of WoD agg Damage wouldn't stop a timelord regeneration event nowadays.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always assumed decapitations, disintegrations, and Gallifreyian-made weaponry were the guaranteed methods to put a TL down for good. Ten's death in Turn Left was attributed to the flames and the flood he unleashed on the Raccnos simply overwhelming him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23581-professordetective","name":"ProfessorDetective","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T05:48:20-07:00","id":1454342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ProfessorDetective</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453418-timelords?p=1454171#post1454171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always assumed decapitations, disintegrations, and Gallifreyian-made weaponry were the guaranteed methods to put a TL down for good. Ten's death in Turn Left was attributed to the flames and the flood he unleashed on the Raccnos simply overwhelming him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Straight up disintergrations and some high tech weapons like the TImelords and timewar Daleks can kill a time lord out right (though even a timewar dalek will only kill with a full hit, they can regenerate from a glancing blow). Decapitations def don't. The issue with drowning or vacume exposure is that the regeneration happens and then the timelord is still stick in the same lethal situation. In particular Ten was practically suicidal at the time and and was secretly the 11 regeneration so only had one left and didn't have enough regenerations to adapt to the presure of the massive flood, depth and needing to breath water. its been confirmed in the books and implied in the tv series that timeords are not restricted to the humanoid (well, galyfrianiod) form, its just the prefered form of their cultural conservatism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T05:49:47-07:00","id":1454444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453418-timelords?p=1454342#post1454342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Straight up disintergrations and some high tech weapons like the TImelords and timewar Daleks can kill a time lord out right (though even a timewar dalek will only kill with a full hit, they can regenerate from a glancing blow). Decapitations def don't. The issue with drowning or vacume exposure is that the regeneration happens and then the timelord is still stick in the same lethal situation. In particular Ten was practically suicidal at the time and and was secretly the 11 regeneration so only had one left and didn't have enough regenerations to adapt to the presure of the massive flood, depth and needing to breath water. its been confirmed in the books and implied in the tv series that timeords are not restricted to the humanoid (well, galyfrianiod) form, its just the prefered form of their cultural conservatism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ten wasn't secretly Eleven at the time. That didn't come until the events of the Stolen Earth at the end of Donna Noble's time in the TARDIS. Russel T Davies was just very inconsistent on what the Doctor could and could not survive. Given the Time Lord respiratory bypass system, drowning isn't even certain to kill the Doctor once let alone kill him for good. On the other hand Time Lords have no special protection from falling damage and yet Ten shrugs off a terminal velocity fall with only minor cuts and scrapes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}